    "title": "Rick Pitino criticized for coaching decision in loss vs. Duke",
    "text": "Less than a week ago, the No. 5 St. John's Red Storm were on top of the world. Dylan Darling hit a buzzer-beater to beat No. 4 Kansas and send St. John's to the Sweet 16 of the men's NCAA Tournament for the first time since 1999.On Friday night, St. John's faced No. 1 Duke and trailed 78-75 as time ticked toward triple zeros. Darling hoisted up a deep three with four seconds remaining, and it landed as an airball with a thud. Sports can be cruel. Duke won 80-75 to advance to the Elite Eight.After the game, college basketball fans wondered why St. John's Hall of Fame head coach Rick Pitino didn't give sophomore forward Ruben Prey a chance to be the Red Storm's unlikely hero. NEW YORK, NEW YORK - MARCH 14: Head coach Rick Pitino of the St. John's Red Storm reacts during the first half of the 2026 Big East Men's Tournament C...Prey was 4-for-4 from 3 for 12 points. With 15:43 left in the second half, Prey made a corner 3 to put St. John's up 53-44, and he didn't attempt another shot again. Prey was yanked from the game with 13:29 to go and didn't return until 32 seconds remained in regulation.\"Rick Pitino is an all-time great coach,\" ESPN's Mike Greenberg posted on X (formerly Twitter). \"But, taking Ruben Prey out of this game is an inexplicable decision.\"Greenberg wrote in another tweet: \"Terrific game, like a prize fight. Duke found a way. But I will never understand why Pitino went away from the hottest hand he had. His players played better than he coached tonight.\"Greenberg wasn't alone in his criticism. John Lund posted a comedic GIF with the caption: \"Ruben Prey when someone asks him after the game why Rick Pitino didn’t play him late in the second half while having the best game of his life.\"Another New York sports fan posted: \"Rick Pitino worst move tonight was not playing Ruben Prey extended minutes.\" Another St. John's fan wrote, \"It’s hard to question Rick Pitino. I know he is one of the best to ever do it, but I just can’t comprehend Ruben Prey basically sitting the rest of the game after hitting his 4th three. Great run Johnnies!\"Even the New York Post promoted its coverage of the St. John's postgame pressers with \"find out why Ruben Prey didn't play in the second half.\"Pitino, who has been at St. John's since 2023, has nothing left to prove, as he's the only Division I men's basketball coach to win national titles at two universities (Kentucky and Louisville). He knows more about college basketball than most anyone questioning his usage of Prey. But this loss will hurt the Johnnies all offseason.",
